diff --git a/experiments/native-tui-execution/README.md b/experiments/native-tui-execution/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a301559
--- /dev/null
+++ b/experiments/native-tui-execution/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# Native TUI execution seam (M1 fixture)
+
+This directory records the smallest reproducible external-execution setup.
+Set `dsh-tui.driverId` to the registered driver id. The TUI then mounts the
+standard Chat and PromptInput around that driver's projection and never calls
+the native `resolveAgent()` path.
+
+`fake-driver.ts` is a deterministic fixture: submit streams an echo, cancel
+marks the in-memory projection idle, and the driver can be disposed repeatedly.
+It is a test fixture, not a production driver. M1 rows are display projection
+only; the external driver remains responsible for any durable transcript.
+
+For a profile row, load `fixture-plugin.ts` after `dsh-tui-extensions` and
+load dsh-tui with `driverId: fixture`. From this checkout, the direct TS
+fixture entry is `node --import tsx/esm experiments/native-tui-execution/fixture-plugin.ts`.
+
+The public driver contract lives in `src/dsh-adapter/session-execution.ts`.
+An external driver owns its execution session; `uiSessionId` is the stable
+conversation identity used by the UI and must not change merely because the
+driver changes a backend execution id.
+
+Unsupported native actions (attachments, shell, steer, fork, model/effort,
+recap, background agents, and native slash commands) remain visibly refused.
+
+M2 adds role-tagged history rows, draft restoration/observation, driver-owned
+commands and monotonic idle session updates. These additions remain generic:
+ARC checkpoints, endpoint configuration, Home and SSH stay inside the optional
+ARC driver. Live turn events remain fenced by the host's turn id. Idle session
+updates are rejected while a submitted turn is active, and older generations
+cannot overwrite a newer handoff. The existing prompt title can display the
+logical session's title; backend changes do not rebind the editor.
+
+A late profile patch replaces `config` wholesale: if it changes TUI options,
+repeat `driverId` explicitly. The selected id must be registered before the UI
+row runs. Composer callbacks travel through an internal scoped context to the
+guarded driver; plugins never obtain React refs or another driver's handle.
